Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_K%C5%8Dgon$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%E5%85%89%E5%8E%B3%E6%B3%95%E7%9A%87%E5%83%8F.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Sovereign$b$, NULL, $b$Jōshōkō-ji Temple$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Kōkō$b$, DATE '0830-01-01', DATE '0887-09-17', $b$Emperor Kōkō (光孝天皇, Kōkō-tennō; 830 – September 17, 887) was the 58th emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession. Kōkō reigned from 884 to 887.

Before the emperor's ascension to the Chrysanthemum Throne, his name (imina) was Tokiyasu Shinnō (時康親王) or Komatsu-tei.  He would later be identified sometimes as "the Emperor of Komatsu". This resulted in the later Emperor Go-Komatsu adopting this name (go- meaning "later", so "Later Emperor Komatsu" or "Emperor Komatsu II"). Kōkō had four Imperial consorts and 41 Imperial sons and daughters.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_K%C5%8Dk%C5%8D$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Tenn%C5%8D%20K%C5%8Dk%C5%8D.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Waka poet, Emperor of Japan$b$, $b$Kyoto$b$, $b$Jijūden$b$, 'year', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Kōnin$b$, DATE '0709-11-18', DATE '0782-01-11', $b$Emperor Kōnin (光仁天皇, Kōnin-tennō; November 18, 708 – January 11, 782) was the 49th emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession. Kōnin's reign lasted from 770 to 781; he reigned during the Nara period.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_K%C5%8Dnin$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emperor%20K%C5%8Dnin.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Ruler$b$, NULL, $b$Heijō-kyō$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Kōtoku$b$, DATE '0596-01-01', DATE '0654-11-24', $b$Emperor Kōtoku (孝徳天皇, Kōtoku-tennō; 596 – 24 November 654) was the 36th emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession.

The years of his reign lasted from 645 through 654.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_K%C5%8Dtoku$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emperor%20Kotoku.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Ruler, Monarch$b$, NULL, $b$Naniwa Nagara-Toyosaki Palace$b$, 'year', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Monmu$b$, DATE '0683-01-01', DATE '0707-07-18', $b$Emperor Monmu (文武天皇, Monmu-tennō; 683–707) was the 42nd emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession.

Monmu's reign spanned the years from 697 through 707.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Monmu$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emperor%20Monmu.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Sovereign$b$, NULL, $b$Fujiwara Palace$b$, 'year', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Montoku$b$, DATE '0827-08-01', DATE '0858-10-07', $b$Emperor Montoku (文徳天皇, Montoku-tennō) (August 827 – 7 October 858) was the 55th emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession.

Montoku's reign lasted from 850 to 858. Before Montoku's ascension to the Chrysanthemum Throne, his personal name (imina) was Michiyasu (道康).  He was also known as Tamura-no-mikado or Tamura-tei. Montoku had six Imperial consorts and 29 Imperial children.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Montoku$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emperor%20Montoku.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Ruler$b$, NULL, $b$Reizen-in$b$, 'month', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Emperor Murakami$b$, DATE '0926-07-14', DATE '0967-07-05', $b$Emperor Murakami (村上天皇, Murakami-tennō; 14 July 924 – 5 July 967) was the 62nd emperor of Japan, according to the traditional order of succession.

